{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And if he has no daughter, then you shall give his inheritance to his brothers.</b> The sage R. Abraham, of blessed memory, explained: brothers from the father's side or brothers from the mother's side, for all of them take precedence over his father's brothers, and needless to say over his mother's brothers. But our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said that the mother's family is not called a family, and brothers from the mother do not inherit one another, but only brothers from the father; if so, his father's brothers take precedence over his brothers from the mother. And the son inherits his mother, but she does not inherit her son — rather, his father's relatives do. And a sister inherits her brother if he has no father and no brother, just as a daughter inherits the father where there is no son. If so, the word לאחיו includes the brother and the sister alike. And after the passage mentioned that the son inherits the father, by the same reasoning the father also inherits the son, but the Torah did not wish to mention this because it is a way of calamity. And it is known that every inheritor also is inherited, for the kinship is equal, and therefore Scripture did not mention this ruling. Or perhaps this never occurred in the world, when they came into the land, that a son would die during the father's lifetime, and therefore Scripture spoke only of what was destined to be practiced among them. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:27.683400145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}